Read palettes in the type gDPSetTextureLUT sets

On the N64, a CI4 or CI8 texel is an index into a palette (TLUT) that G_LOADTLUT copied into TMEM, and the RDP reads
the type of the palette's entries from other_mode_h's TEXTLUT field (gDPSetTextureLUT) as it draws: G_TT_RGBA16
entries are RGBA5551 colours, G_TT_IA16 entries an 8-bit intensity (high byte) and an 8-bit alpha (low byte). Fast3D
never read the field and decoded every palette as RGBA5551, so an IA16 palette came out in the wrong colours, each
pixel either opaque or invisible. WCW/nWo Revenge draws its effect sprites and its HUD quads with IA16 palettes: it
sends G_SETOTHERMODE_H E3001001 0000C000 (IA16) before their triangles and E3001001 00008000 (RGBA16) after them.

ImportTextureCi4 and ImportTextureCi8 (which also decode the CI textures of resources loaded as raw) now read the type
and decode each entry with DecodePaletteEntry: an IA16 entry gives red, green and blue equal to its intensity, and its
own alpha; RGBA16, and G_TT_NONE as before, give RGBA5551. The type is also part of the texture cache's key
(TextureCacheKey::palette_ia16), because the same texels and palette, at the same addresses, make a different texture
in each type. And because the RDP applies the type as it draws, a G_SETOTHERMODE_H or G_RDPSETOTHERMODE that changes
it marks both textures as changed, so the next triangle imports them again for the new type instead of drawing with
the ones decoded for the old.

Not in LibUltraShip main on 2026-11-08; drop this patch once it is there.

diff --git a/include/fast/interpreter.h b/include/fast/interpreter.h
index 1ff55a8a..ed789456 100644
--- a/include/fast/interpreter.h
+++ b/include/fast/interpreter.h
@@ -190,6 +190,10 @@ struct TextureCacheKey {
     uint8_t fmt, siz;
     uint8_t palette_index;
     uint32_t size_bytes;
+    // CI textures only: the palette was read as IA16 (G_TT_IA16) rather than RGBA16. The same texels and palette give
+    // other colours in each type, so each type needs an entry of its own. It comes last, so keys built without it (all
+    // the other formats) get false.
+    bool palette_ia16;
 
     bool operator==(const TextureCacheKey&) const noexcept = default;
 
